        "Abstract": "We introduce the GoEmotions dataset, a human-annotated dataset of 58k Reddit comments labeled for 27 emotion categories or Neutral. The emotions are chosen based on a survey of existing emotion frameworks in emotion research. We report on the creation of the dataset and its baseline performance using a variety of neural architectures. We also present a transfer learning experiment showing that GoEmotions can be used to improve performance on other emotion datasets."
